.SH NAME
multi_select \- a dropdown that picks any number of options
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
MultiSelect::new(options: &'a [T], selected: &'a [T], on_toggle: impl Fn(T) \-> M + 'a)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBMultiSelect\fR: a dropdown that picks any number of options.
.PP
The same popover and option rows as \fBdropdown\fR (they share \fBoption_items\fR), but the popover stays open while options are toggled and the trigger shows the chosen values as \fBChip\fR\-like pills, \fB+n\fR when more than \fBmax_chips\fR. State is controlled: pass the current selection and turn \fBon_toggle(option)\fR into your own update. The trigger's pills are display\-only (the trigger toggles the popover); remove a value by toggling it in the list.
.PP
\fBselecting\fR takes the new list instead of one toggled option, computed by the shared \fBSelection\fR rule, which also gives a single\-choice variant (\fBSelection::SINGLE\fR) with the same widget.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.TP
.B MultiSelect::new(options: &'a [T], selected: &'a [T], on_toggle: impl Fn(T) \-> M + 'a)
.TP
.B MultiSelect::selecting(options: &'a [T], selected: &'a [T], rule: crate::primitives::Selection, on_change: impl Fn(Vec<T>) \-> M + 'a)
Like \fBnew\fR, but \fBon_change\fR receives the whole new selection, worked out by \fBrule\fR (\fBSelection::Multiple\fR for any number).
